      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SHAHAR (2) has been about the mark at all five runs this prep, almost breaking through last start when beaten a head over this distance at the Sunshine Coast. Boasts a win and three placings from four runs at Toowoomba. This gives her a great chance to get the monkey off her back. HOLD MY HAND (5) ran a nice race here first-up over 1015m then might have been looking for more ground when fourth over the same trip at the Sunny Coast last time. Comes right under notice over this longer journey. DAIANE (1) lined up for only the second time and registered an effortless all-the-way win over this course and distance recently. Promising mare who certainly looks up to this better company. HAWAIIAN BLOOM (3) streeted a maiden field over 1300m here two runs back before crashing back to earth at Beaudesert last time. Worth another chance.",
